From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: macbox <macbox@localhost>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:36:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 40/92] the flat variant stays SIMD16 and counts a 1-D
 workgroup from its id

The flat variant's index math gets three arms, each chosen by workgroup-uniform values:
a workgroup of the first row and layer whose last index is below 2^32 counts in 32 bits
from wx*N (no NumWorkgroups read, which ANV merges per invocation); any other workgroup of
a dispatch of at most 2^32 invocations counts in 32 bits as before; past that the 64-bit
index is divided by a compact 64/32 restoring loop instead of 64-bit OpUDiv/OpUMod. The
position is derived once, for the guard and thread_position_in_grid.

On Arrow Lake (Mesa 26.2) the four lowered 64-bit divisions in the unexecuted arm made
the Simulator's masked blit compile at SIMD8 (2801 instructions); it now compiles at
SIMD16 (346). Apple's metallib through the runtime, 10 paired rounds against 5f6f2c9f in
both orders: p50 1.88 -> 1.54 ms, min 1.50 -> 1.40 ms, faster in 10 of 10, outputs
byte-identical. The bare kernel in the lab shows no difference (p50 1.17 vs 1.21 ms,
inside the spread).

Tests: interpreter test of the 64/32 division over edge dividends and divisors; GPU lane
for a dispatch past 2^32 threads in 105-thread groups, where the 32- to 64-bit switch
lands inside a row.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
